# Comparator web daemon supervision — no systemd available on this host (no
# usable `systemctl --user`, no sudo for a system-level unit), so cron plays
# the restart-on-crash/start-on-boot role instead. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# Install with `crontab -e`, adjusting REPO_DIR if your checkout moves.
#
# Start the daemon on boot:
@reboot         /home/grads/scripts/python/rtc/DAG_ModelComparison-reduced_compute/deploy/run_dag_server.sh
#
# Restart it if it stops answering (5-minute worst-case detection window):
*/5 * * * *     /home/grads/scripts/python/rtc/DAG_ModelComparison-reduced_compute/deploy/watchdog_dag_server.sh
#
# Delete GRIB2 downloads, their .idx index files, and generated PNG/GIF figures
# older than 24h so the disk does not grow without bound. Runs hourly at :17
# (offset from the watchdog); the schedule frequency is independent of the 24h
# retention window baked into the script. Spares the regridder weight cache
# (weights_*_knn.npz) and the runs.jsonl manifest. Pass a different retention,
# e.g. `... cleanup_dag_files.sh 48`, to keep two days instead.
17 * * * *      /home/grads/scripts/python/rtc/DAG_ModelComparison-reduced_compute/deploy/cleanup_dag_files.sh
